templateVersions.content:
A Brightline Home Comfort technician dictated these notes during a system check: "{!$Input:Notes}"
{!$Input:Context}
Turn the notes into one finding. Use only values from the allowed lists, exactly as written, or null when the notes don't say. Keep the equipment the technician is at unless the notes name a different one. Copy any make, model number, serial number, install year and measured reading (with its unit) the notes mention; leave them null otherwise. Urgency: Monitor for normal wear, Repair Soon for a part that is failing or out of spec, Safety for carbon monoxide, gas, a cracked heat exchanger or electrical hazards.
Reply with only a JSON object, no other text: {"equipment": "...", "component": "...", "condition": "...", "urgency": "...", "make": "brand or null", "modelNumber": "model number or null", "serialNumber": "serial number or null", "installYear": "four-digit year or null", "reading": "measured value with its unit, such as 32 µF or 68 psi, or null", "customerNote": "one or two plain sentences for the homeowner", "internalNote": "technical details for the next technician (readings, part numbers, access, follow-ups) or null"}
